	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: [ ]
			description: [
				"This book walks the mod's progression from the first fire to the dye works. Each quest names a goal and the idea behind it. It never gives a layout: how you build each step is up to you."
				""
				"Three things carry the details. JEI shows every recipe and the heat, speed or charge it needs. Ponder shows how a block behaves: hover over an item and hold W. Create's Engineer's Goggles show what a placed block is doing, from a Furnace's heat to a shaft's limits."
				""
				"An item quest ticks itself once the item is in your inventory. If one hasn't, click the task to check."
			]
			icon: "minecraft:writable_book"
			id: "1626CEC5328F5382"
			rewards: [ ]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "How this book works"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "50A6BEBC1E63857E"
					title: "Got it"
					type: "checkmark"
				}
			]
			title: "Welcome to the Remix"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"1626CEC5328F5382"
			]
			description: [
				"Vanilla's furnace, smoker and blast furnace have gone cold: their menus stay shut and they smelt nothing, even fed by hoppers."
				""
				"Food cooks on a campfire. Later, an Encased Fan blowing through fire smokes food in bulk."
			]
			id: "2A24C5248E6A15BB"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Vanilla's furnaces have gone cold"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "73EB0FD6094F38CE"
					item: "minecraft:campfire"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Food Goes on the Fire"
			x: 1.75d
			y: -1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"1626CEC5328F5382"
			]
			description: [
				"Vanilla's furnace recipe still makes one, but it is the Furnace now. It has no menu: click things to fire into its upper chamber and fuel into its low firebox, and watch them sit on the grate, glow and wait to be taken out."
				""
				"Hoppers and funnels work it too: things to fire go in at the top, fuel at the sides, and results come out of the bottom. It refuses food."
				""
				"&7Ponder: the Furnace.&r"
			]
			id: "6C06A8D2FE2265D4"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "No menu, and a cut-open front"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "29AA74CA6B016190"
					item: "mcremix:kiln"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "The Furnace"
			x: 1.75d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"6C06A8D2FE2265D4"
			]
			description: [
				"Fuel in the firebox doesn't catch by itself. Flint and steel or a fire charge lights it, by hand or from a Deployer. Flint and steel takes iron, and iron comes later in this book, so look for your first lighter: a ruined portal's chest can hold flint and steel or a fire charge, and mineshafts, dungeons and shipwrecks still keep iron."
				""
				"Once lit, it burns its fuel to the end whether or not it has work, so load it when you mean to use it. A shovel puts it out and leaves the fuel in for next time."
				""
				"Heat from the block underneath needs no lighting at all."
			]
			id: "380C39E07B5A7809"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Fuel waits for a flame"
			tasks: [
				{
					icon: "minecraft:flint_and_steel"
					id: "56F5E09C159A870B"
					observe_type: 2
					timer: 10L
					title: "Look at a lit Furnace"
					to_observe: "mcremix:kiln[lit=true]"
					type: "observation"
				}
			]
			title: "Light It"
			x: 3.5d
			y: 1.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"6C06A8D2FE2265D4"
			]
			description: [
				"Everything that cooks or fires shares one scale: &eWarm&r, &6Hot&r, &cSearing&r and &bBlazing&r. Each recipe needs a least heat, and every level above it halves the time."
				""
				"Wood fuel burns only &eWarm&r, as does a campfire or magma block under the Furnace. That is enough to char logs into charcoal and to fire clay into bricks and terracotta. A Furnace on a campfire stays &eWarm&r forever with no fuel."
				""
				"&7JEI: the Furnace tab gives each firing's heat, and the Furnace Heat tab shows what burns how hot.&r"
			]
			id: "466E58C303880A27"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "One scale for every fire"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "5CBE8993824B8BDB"
					item: "minecraft:charcoal"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Warm: Charcoal"
			x: 3.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"466E58C303880A27"
				"380C39E07B5A7809"
			]
			description: [
				"Charcoal and coal burn &6Hot&r, and so does fire or lava under the Furnace. &6Hot&r does vanilla's smelting that isn't food, such as glass, smooth stone, copper and gold. Raw iron, iron ore and ancient debris are the exceptions: they now need hotter firings of their own."
				""
				"Copper is the first metal you'll work, for Create's parts and the first tier of your own."
			]
			id: "690A67A6D21199B1"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Charcoal and coal burn Hot"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "75C181D5C84656E9"
					item: "minecraft:glass"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "66D678EA48FD0477"
					item: "minecraft:copper_ingot"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "Hot: Glass and Copper"
			x: 5.25d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: [
				"690A67A6D21199B1"
			]
			description: [
				"Coal fired &6Hot&r cokes into Coal Coke, which burns &cSearing&r and lasts twice as long as coal."
				""
				"Coking also gives off coal tar into a small tank in the Furnace. You can ignore it for now: past a bucket's worth it burns away at the chimney. Later it becomes one of the most useful things you make."
			]
			id: "35D075A91FFA3F0D"
			rewards: [ ]
			subtitle: "Coal baked hotter"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "3E64DF6DF16C8B4E"
